{% if organize %}
Decide how to investigate the question after the initial search. When it names several distinct
outcomes or asks for separate comparisons, create one independent research stream per
main part, up to four. Keep named outcomes separate when there are four or fewer.
Give each stream a short topic name and a dedicated query that would surface evidence on that part alone.
Carry any named entity, location, document or other scope constraint into the query.
Put at least one concrete measure, mechanism or distinctive term from the question in the query.
Avoid generic seeds such as "factors influencing outcomes".
Avoid repeating the full user question or changing only the word order. Return only JSON
with key "streams" and two to four items, each containing "topic" and "query". Include
"geographic_scope" with the geographic scope the user specified, or an empty string if none.
For example, {"streams":[{"topic":"Reliability","query":"reported failures and operating conditions"},
{"topic":"Costs","query":"maintenance costs and cost per use"}],"geographic_scope":""}.
For a single inquiry, use the follow-up format below instead.
